 ## Background
-The concept of source-attenuation reprojection originates from work by Vannier et al. in the context of stereotactic neurosurgery planning [S1, unofficial]. The polynomial composition methods are described in unofficial notes regarding efficient numerical evaluation in volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. These techniques are used in direct volume visualization pipelines where accurate field evaluation or resampling is critical for image quality.
